WEBVTT

00:00:01.019 --> 00:00:12.628
The House on the Hill by Elizabeth Laird.

00:00:12.687 --> 00:00:25.977
Part 1 It was a beautiful summer evening.

00:00:26.037 --> 00:00:27.940
Paul was happy.

00:00:28.001 --> 00:00:29.994
No more exams.

00:00:30.054 --> 00:00:32.046
College was finished.

00:00:32.107 --> 00:00:34.968
Now he needed a job.

00:00:35.028 --> 00:00:39.382
He wanted to be a writer and work for a newspaper.

00:00:39.442 --> 00:00:42.695
But first he needed a rest.

00:00:42.755 --> 00:00:44.766
It was hot in the house.

00:00:44.826 --> 00:00:46.778
There was no wind.

00:00:46.838 --> 00:00:50.592
I'll go for a walk, said Paul to himself.

00:00:50.652 --> 00:00:53.950
I'll go down to the river.

00:00:54.010 --> 00:01:00.067
Paul lived in a small town and he was soon outside in the country.

00:01:00.127 --> 00:01:04.228
He walked near the river and watched the water birds.

00:01:04.288 --> 00:01:08.010
Suddenly he saw the girl.

00:01:08.070 --> 00:01:12.041
She was standing alone, looking into the water.

00:01:12.101 --> 00:01:15.702
She was young and very beautiful.

00:01:15.762 --> 00:01:21.154
She had long dark hair and she was wearing a pretty white dress.

00:01:21.214 --> 00:01:23.974
Paul went up to her.

00:01:24.034 --> 00:01:27.256
Hello, he said.

00:01:27.316 --> 00:01:29.516
What's your name?

00:01:29.576 --> 00:01:34.538
I'm Maria, she said, and she smiled at him.

00:01:34.598 --> 00:01:38.218
Paul and Maria talked for a long time.

00:01:38.278 --> 00:01:40.229
The sun went down.

00:01:40.289 --> 00:01:42.330
It was nearly dark.

00:01:42.390 --> 00:01:45.731
I must go home, said Maria.

00:01:45.791 --> 00:01:49.052
Where do you live, asked Paul?

00:01:49.111 --> 00:01:52.813
In the big white house on the hill, said Maria.

00:01:52.873 --> 00:01:54.414
Where do you live?

00:01:54.474 --> 00:01:58.527
in the little brown house near the market said Paul.

00:01:58.586 --> 00:02:02.600
They laughed, but Paul was sad.

00:02:02.660 --> 00:02:06.292
The house on the hill was big and important.

00:02:06.352 --> 00:02:13.388
Maria was rich, and he was poor, and Paul was in love.

00:02:13.448 --> 00:02:18.072
After that, Paul and Maria often met near the river.

00:02:18.132 --> 00:02:21.394
Maria always wore beautiful clothes.

00:02:21.454 --> 00:02:24.012
She always looked lovely.

00:02:24.072 --> 00:02:29.348
Paul thought about Maria all day and every day.

00:02:29.408 --> 00:02:36.439
One evening Paul said, listen Maria, I've written a poem about you.

00:02:36.499 --> 00:02:41.580
He took a piece of paper from his pocket and read the poem.

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:45.911
I met her in the evening by the river side.

00:02:45.971 --> 00:02:51.466
Her dress was creamy white and her hair with ribbon tied.

00:02:51.526 --> 00:02:56.582
She turned and smiled at me, and I asked her for her name.

00:02:56.642 --> 00:03:02.208
Though I am young and poor, my love will stay the same.

00:03:02.267 --> 00:03:05.930
You are wonderful, Paul, said Maria.

00:03:05.990 --> 00:03:08.002
I love your poem.

00:03:08.062 --> 00:03:10.654
Paul took Maria's hand.

00:03:10.714 --> 00:03:12.906
He looked into her eyes.

00:03:12.966 --> 00:03:15.890
I love you, Maria, he said.

00:03:15.950 --> 00:03:17.860
Do you love me?

00:03:17.920 --> 00:03:19.611
She smiled.

00:03:19.671 --> 00:03:23.862
Yes, of course I love you," she said.

00:03:23.921 --> 00:03:25.542
She stood up.

00:03:25.602 --> 00:03:27.762
I must go home now.

00:03:27.822 --> 00:03:30.644
Paul was very happy.

00:03:30.704 --> 00:03:32.724
She loves me.

00:03:32.784 --> 00:03:36.546
Maria loves me, he thought.

00:03:36.606 --> 00:03:39.296
Paul went home.

00:03:39.356 --> 00:03:42.578
The little brown house was small and poor.

00:03:42.638 --> 00:03:45.669
But it was always clean and tidy.

00:03:45.728 --> 00:03:48.440
Paul lived alone with his mother.

00:03:48.499 --> 00:03:50.344
His father was dead.

00:03:50.404 --> 00:03:53.728
That evening, his mother watched him.

00:03:53.788 --> 00:03:55.888
What's happened, Paul?

00:03:55.948 --> 00:03:56.969
She asked.

00:03:57.029 --> 00:03:59.590
Why are you so happy?

00:03:59.650 --> 00:04:03.281
Oh, it's nothing, mother, said Paul.

00:04:03.340 --> 00:04:05.341
His mother smiled.

00:04:05.401 --> 00:04:09.092
He's in love, she thought.

00:04:09.152 --> 00:04:14.044
The next day, Paul and Maria met again by the river.

00:04:14.104 --> 00:04:17.935
Maria looked sad, but Paul did not notice.

00:04:17.995 --> 00:04:19.951
He took her hand.

00:04:20.010 --> 00:04:22.357
Maria, he said.

00:04:22.416 --> 00:04:27.548
I am poor now, but one day I am going to be a famous writer.

00:04:27.608 --> 00:04:30.089
Maria said nothing.

00:04:30.149 --> 00:04:32.400
Will you marry me, Maria?

00:04:32.460 --> 00:04:33.510
Say yes.

00:04:33.570 --> 00:04:36.201
We will be so happy and...

00:04:36.261 --> 00:04:38.032
he stopped.

00:04:38.092 --> 00:04:40.682
Maria looked at him for a moment.

00:04:40.742 --> 00:04:43.053
There were tears in her eyes.

00:04:43.113 --> 00:04:45.884
Slowly, she shook her head.

00:04:45.944 --> 00:04:48.594
Then she turned and ran away.

00:04:48.654 --> 00:04:50.134
Maria!

00:04:50.194 --> 00:04:51.623
Chatted Paul.

00:04:51.683 --> 00:04:54.124
But Maria had gone.

00:04:54.184 --> 00:04:56.636
Paul went home slowly.

00:04:56.696 --> 00:04:59.328
He did not understand Maria.

00:04:59.388 --> 00:05:01.980
What is wrong, he thought.

00:05:02.040 --> 00:05:05.352
She loves me, doesn't she?

00:05:05.412 --> 00:05:09.134
His mother was waiting for him.

00:05:09.194 --> 00:05:11.646
She saw his face.

00:05:11.706 --> 00:05:14.809
Oh, poor boy, she thought.

00:05:14.869 --> 00:05:18.117
The girl doesn't love him.

00:05:18.177 --> 00:05:22.776
Paul and his mother ate their supper in silence.

00:05:22.836 --> 00:05:25.820
Suddenly somebody knocked on the door.

00:05:25.880 --> 00:05:27.530
Paul opened it.

00:05:27.590 --> 00:05:30.323
A man in a servant's uniform stood outside.

00:05:30.343 --> 00:05:33.886
"'I'm from the house on the hill,' he said.

00:05:33.906 --> 00:05:35.848
"'My mistress wants to see Paul.'

00:05:35.868 --> 00:05:38.630
"'Oh, that's me,' said Paul.

00:05:38.650 --> 00:05:40.802
"'Can you come with me now?'

00:05:40.862 --> 00:05:41.713
said the servant.

00:05:41.733 --> 00:05:44.806
"'Yes,' said Paul.

00:05:44.866 --> 00:05:46.598
He was excited.

00:05:46.658 --> 00:05:50.301
Perhaps Maria has changed her mind, he thought.

00:05:50.361 --> 00:05:53.132
Perhaps she does want to marry me.

00:05:53.192 --> 00:05:56.352
Paul's mother stood at the door of the house.

00:05:56.412 --> 00:05:58.993
She watched Paul and the servant.

00:05:59.053 --> 00:06:02.624
The house on the hill, she said to herself.

00:06:02.684 --> 00:06:04.754
I know those people.

00:06:04.814 --> 00:06:10.976
A rich old woman, and her beautiful daughter, my poor son.

00:06:11.035 --> 00:06:14.204
It was not far to the house on the hill.

00:06:14.264 --> 00:06:18.626
The servant took Paul up the wide steps and into the house.

00:06:18.686 --> 00:06:23.540
Paul was excited, and his heart was beating fast.

00:06:23.600 --> 00:06:26.593
Everything was rich and grand.

00:06:26.653 --> 00:06:30.656
There were beautiful carpets, pictures and mirrors.

00:06:30.716 --> 00:06:33.408
Paul saw himself in a mirror.

00:06:33.468 --> 00:06:35.670
He looked terrible.

00:06:35.730 --> 00:06:40.765
This place was so rich, and he looked so poor.

00:06:40.825 --> 00:06:43.363
The servant opened a door.

00:06:43.423 --> 00:06:45.511
Paul went inside.

00:06:45.570 --> 00:06:48.713
An old lady was sitting in a big chair.

00:06:48.773 --> 00:06:51.044
Maria stood behind her.

00:06:51.104 --> 00:06:53.306
The old woman was ugly.

00:06:53.366 --> 00:06:58.732
Her eyes were small and cold, and her mouth was thin and hard.

00:06:58.792 --> 00:07:02.064
Her old hands were covered with big rings.

00:07:02.124 --> 00:07:05.436
She looked proud and angry.

00:07:05.496 --> 00:07:09.500
Paul looked at the old woman, then at Maria.

00:07:09.559 --> 00:07:12.622
What an ugly old woman, he thought.

00:07:12.682 --> 00:07:14.793
Is she Maria's mother?

00:07:14.853 --> 00:07:18.825
So, you want to marry my daughter?

00:07:18.885 --> 00:07:20.466
The old woman said.

00:07:20.526 --> 00:07:22.507
Her voice was hard.

00:07:22.567 --> 00:07:25.138
Paul looked at her bravely.

00:07:25.198 --> 00:07:27.280
Yes, he said.

00:07:27.340 --> 00:07:30.591
I love Maria, and I want to marry her.

00:07:30.651 --> 00:07:32.702
The old woman laughed.

00:07:32.762 --> 00:07:35.684
You are a poor student.

00:07:35.744 --> 00:07:38.515
No money, no father, nothing.

00:07:38.575 --> 00:07:42.454
My daughter will never marry you.

00:07:42.514 --> 00:07:44.792
Paul said nothing.

00:07:44.852 --> 00:07:46.773
He looked at Maria.

00:07:46.833 --> 00:07:49.234
She did not look at him.

00:07:49.294 --> 00:07:55.538
I am poor now, he said, but one day I'll be a famous writer.

00:07:55.597 --> 00:07:57.909
The old woman laughed again.

00:07:57.969 --> 00:08:00.160
No, she said.

00:08:00.220 --> 00:08:03.312
My daughter is not for you.

00:08:03.371 --> 00:08:06.173
She is going to be married soon.

00:08:06.233 --> 00:08:11.278
You will never see her again.

00:08:11.338 --> 00:08:15.542
The old woman got up and left the room.

00:08:15.602 --> 00:08:18.405
Maria and Paul were alone.

00:08:18.464 --> 00:08:23.168
Paul looked at Maria, but she did not look at him.

00:08:23.228 --> 00:08:26.992
She stood still and did not say anything.

00:08:27.052 --> 00:08:30.934
Paul went up to her and put his arm around her.

00:08:30.994 --> 00:08:33.736
Maria moved away from him.

00:08:33.796 --> 00:08:37.130
I'm sorry, Paul, said Maria.

00:08:37.189 --> 00:08:39.100
My mother is right.

00:08:39.161 --> 00:08:41.056
I can't marry you.

00:08:41.116 --> 00:08:43.240
I don't want to be Paul.

00:08:43.300 --> 00:08:47.302
I want money and clothes and a big car.

00:08:47.362 --> 00:08:52.514
But you love me, Maria," said Paul, and I love you.

00:08:52.574 --> 00:08:54.796
He did not understand her.

00:08:54.856 --> 00:08:56.826
He was angry.

00:08:56.887 --> 00:09:01.179
Yes, I love you, Paul," said Maria.

00:09:01.239 --> 00:09:03.820
But love isn't enough.

00:09:03.880 --> 00:09:05.572
She looked at him.

00:09:05.632 --> 00:09:07.892
Her face was sad.

00:09:07.952 --> 00:09:10.863
I'm getting married in two weeks.

00:09:10.923 --> 00:09:13.643
She said, goodbye, Paul.

00:09:13.703 --> 00:09:15.814
I'm sorry.

00:09:15.873 --> 00:09:20.995
Paul left the big house and ran down the hill to the river.

00:09:21.055 --> 00:09:23.996
He sat there for a long time.

00:09:24.056 --> 00:09:26.417
Maria loves me.

00:09:26.477 --> 00:09:29.208
I know she loves me, he thought.

00:09:29.268 --> 00:09:32.318
But she is marrying another man.

00:09:32.378 --> 00:09:35.280
She is marrying him for money.

00:09:35.340 --> 00:09:37.180
It's her mother.

00:09:37.240 --> 00:09:40.764
Maria is afraid of that ugly old woman.

00:09:40.824 --> 00:09:42.507
Oh Maria!

00:09:42.567 --> 00:09:44.018
Maria!

00:09:44.078 --> 00:09:46.480
What shall I do?

00:09:46.540 --> 00:09:50.464
After a long time, Paul went home.

00:09:50.524 --> 00:09:53.406
There was a light in the window of the little house.

00:09:53.466 --> 00:09:55.327
The door was open.

00:09:55.387 --> 00:09:57.789
His mother was waiting for him.

00:09:57.849 --> 00:09:59.610
She looked at his face.

00:09:59.670 --> 00:10:03.013
Then she put her arms around him.

00:10:03.073 --> 00:10:07.746
They are bad people, my son, she said.

00:10:07.806 --> 00:10:18.406
You must forget her.

00:10:18.466 --> 00:10:33.576
Part 2 For many days Paul did not see any of his friends.

00:10:33.636 --> 00:10:35.957
His mother was worried about him.

00:10:36.017 --> 00:10:37.928
He did not talk to her.

00:10:37.988 --> 00:10:40.679
He did not eat or sleep.

00:10:40.739 --> 00:10:44.210
He often went to the river and sat there alone.

00:10:44.270 --> 00:10:47.723
All the time he thought about Maria.

00:10:47.782 --> 00:10:55.685
One day he saw a headline in the newspaper, rich man's beautiful bride.

00:10:55.746 --> 00:11:00.307
There was a picture of Maria and her husband.

00:11:00.367 --> 00:11:04.978
She was wearing a long white dress and a diamond necklace.

00:11:05.038 --> 00:11:08.049
Her husband was old and fat.

00:11:08.109 --> 00:11:11.710
Paul turned the newspaper over angrily.

00:11:11.770 --> 00:11:15.422
There was a large notice on the back page of the newspaper.

00:11:15.482 --> 00:11:17.420
It was an advertisement.

00:11:17.480 --> 00:11:21.708
Paul sat down and read the advertisement carefully.

00:11:21.768 --> 00:11:27.020
Story Competition Write a story and win a prize.

00:11:27.080 --> 00:11:33.811
Our story competition offers a chance to young writers to win recognition and earn money.

00:11:33.871 --> 00:11:39.862
Stories can be on any theme but must not be longer than 1500 words.

00:11:39.922 --> 00:11:44.432
Send your entry to this newspaper before the end of the month.

00:11:44.493 --> 00:11:47.755
First prize, £500.

00:11:47.815 --> 00:11:51.428
ten other prizes of fifty pounds.

00:11:51.488 --> 00:11:54.869
This is my chance, he said to himself.

00:11:54.929 --> 00:12:00.940
I'll write the story of Paul and Maria, and I'll win the competition.

00:12:01.000 --> 00:12:05.402
She'll read our story, and she'll be sorry."

00:12:05.462 --> 00:12:08.192
Paul was very busy now.

00:12:08.252 --> 00:12:11.774
Every day he got up early and worked at his story.

00:12:11.834 --> 00:12:13.674
His mother watched him.

00:12:13.734 --> 00:12:15.184
She was pleased.

00:12:15.244 --> 00:12:17.405
He was eating his food again.

00:12:17.465 --> 00:12:20.196
He was talking and smiling.

00:12:20.256 --> 00:12:23.838
Sometimes Paul felt pleased with his story.

00:12:23.898 --> 00:12:25.888
It was a good story.

00:12:25.948 --> 00:12:29.360
But sometimes it was difficult to write.

00:12:29.420 --> 00:12:33.111
He was unhappy, and he wanted to stop writing.

00:12:33.171 --> 00:12:35.262
But he did not stop.

00:12:35.322 --> 00:12:38.464
At last the story was finished.

00:12:38.524 --> 00:12:40.734
Paul read it to his mother.

00:12:40.794 --> 00:12:43.151
She was very pleased.

00:12:43.211 --> 00:12:46.869
It's a good story, Paul," she said.

00:12:46.929 --> 00:12:48.970
It's very good.

00:12:49.030 --> 00:12:55.594
Paul wrote the story out again carefully and sent it to the newspaper.

00:12:55.654 --> 00:13:01.168
Two weeks later, a letter came from the newspaper.

00:13:01.228 --> 00:13:03.259
Paul did not open it.

00:13:03.319 --> 00:13:05.160
He was too excited.

00:13:05.220 --> 00:13:07.462
He gave it to his mother.

00:13:07.522 --> 00:13:10.704
You read it for me, mother, he said.

00:13:10.764 --> 00:13:14.241
His mother opened the letter and read it.

00:13:14.301 --> 00:13:16.448
Read it yourself!"

00:13:16.508 --> 00:13:18.760
she said, and gave it to him.

00:13:18.820 --> 00:13:21.942
She was laughing and crying too.

00:13:22.002 --> 00:13:24.284
Paul read the letter.

00:13:24.344 --> 00:13:32.190
Dear sir, I am very happy to inform you that you have won first prize in the story competition.

00:13:32.250 --> 00:13:40.386
If you would kindly call at this office on Thursday at 10 a.m., the manager will present you with your prize.

00:13:40.446 --> 00:13:47.066
Paul jumped up He danced round the kitchen and waved the letter from the newspaper.

00:13:47.126 --> 00:13:49.566
I've won, he shouted.

00:13:49.626 --> 00:13:51.777
Mother, I've got the prize.

00:13:51.837 --> 00:13:53.448
I'll be a writer.

00:13:53.508 --> 00:13:55.828
We'll have some money at last.

00:13:55.888 --> 00:14:00.780
I'll buy you a new dress and some furniture for the house.

00:14:00.840 --> 00:14:02.841
He stopped.

00:14:02.901 --> 00:14:06.032
Will Maria see my story in the paper?

00:14:06.092 --> 00:14:07.342
He asked.

00:14:07.402 --> 00:14:09.404
His mother looked at him.

00:14:09.464 --> 00:14:12.018
She was not smiling now.

00:14:12.078 --> 00:14:14.944
Do you still love that girl, Paul?"

00:14:15.004 --> 00:14:16.354
she asked.

00:14:16.414 --> 00:14:18.976
Yes, mother, said Paul.

00:14:19.036 --> 00:14:21.998
I'll always love her.

00:14:22.058 --> 00:14:26.820
On Thursday, Paul went to the newspaper office.

00:14:26.880 --> 00:14:29.640
The manager was very friendly.

00:14:29.700 --> 00:14:32.902
Your story is good, he said.

00:14:32.962 --> 00:14:34.824
Very good indeed.

00:14:34.884 --> 00:14:37.074
Here is the prize money.

00:14:37.134 --> 00:14:39.596
He gave Paul an envelope.

00:14:39.656 --> 00:14:42.512
Five hundred pounds.

00:14:42.572 --> 00:14:44.670
Paul did not believe it.

00:14:44.730 --> 00:14:47.942
He thanked the manager and started to go.

00:14:48.002 --> 00:14:50.654
Don't go, said the manager.

00:14:50.714 --> 00:14:52.305
I want to talk to you.

00:14:52.365 --> 00:14:54.336
What's your job?

00:14:54.397 --> 00:14:57.679
I haven't got a job, sir, said Paul.

00:14:57.739 --> 00:14:59.690
I want to be a writer.

00:14:59.750 --> 00:15:02.072
Good, said the manager.

00:15:02.132 --> 00:15:04.174
We need young men like you.

00:15:04.234 --> 00:15:06.836
Come and work on our newspaper.

00:15:06.896 --> 00:15:09.548
Paul was very surprised.

00:15:09.608 --> 00:15:13.181
You want me on your newspaper?

00:15:13.241 --> 00:15:20.330
Yes, yes, of course I'll come, he said.

00:15:20.390 --> 00:15:35.622
This is Paul, our new reporter.

00:15:35.682 --> 00:15:50.198
Any more news, sir?

00:15:50.258 --> 00:15:58.472
You're working hard, Paul.

00:15:58.532 --> 00:16:07.006
I like your new story, Paul.

00:16:07.066 --> 00:16:22.104
We are very pleased with your work, Paul.

00:16:22.164 --> 00:16:36.010
Part 3 Paul loved his work on the newspaper.

00:16:36.070 --> 00:16:40.522
He worked hard, but he did not forget Maria.

00:16:40.582 --> 00:16:47.552
One day, a reporter came into the office, Listen everybody, he said.

00:16:47.612 --> 00:16:49.732
Here's a story for the paper.

00:16:49.792 --> 00:16:54.384
Do you remember that beautiful girl Maria and her rich husband?

00:16:54.444 --> 00:16:57.775
There was a photograph of the wedding in our paper.

00:16:57.835 --> 00:17:01.536
She ran away from her husband last week.

00:17:01.596 --> 00:17:04.617
Everybody in the office stopped talking.

00:17:04.677 --> 00:17:06.678
This was news.

00:17:06.738 --> 00:17:08.848
Paul sat still.

00:17:08.908 --> 00:17:10.999
He felt cold.

00:17:11.059 --> 00:17:14.718
Maria left her husband, he thought.

00:17:14.779 --> 00:17:16.067
Why?

00:17:16.128 --> 00:17:19.130
They were married only a few months ago.

00:17:19.190 --> 00:17:21.802
The reporter was still talking.

00:17:21.862 --> 00:17:25.625
The girl's mother died last week, he said.

00:17:25.685 --> 00:17:29.558
She heard the news and the shock killed her.

00:17:29.618 --> 00:17:33.752
That ugly old woman thought Paul.

00:17:33.812 --> 00:17:36.604
The mother was rich, wasn't she?

00:17:36.664 --> 00:17:38.164
Somebody asked.

00:17:38.224 --> 00:17:42.787
Oh yes, she was very rich, said the reporter.

00:17:42.847 --> 00:17:45.687
Maria will have all her money, of course.

00:17:45.747 --> 00:17:51.328
And her husband gave her a lot of money, clothes, jewels, and a car.

00:17:51.388 --> 00:17:56.129
Maria is a very, very rich woman.

00:17:56.189 --> 00:17:59.070
Why don't light rich women?

00:17:59.130 --> 00:18:01.350
Said another reporter.

00:18:01.410 --> 00:18:07.862
Maria is rich, said Paul, but she is also gentle and kind and...

00:18:07.922 --> 00:18:09.842
he stopped.

00:18:09.903 --> 00:18:11.981
Do you know Maria?

00:18:12.041 --> 00:18:13.940
The reporter asked.

00:18:14.000 --> 00:18:17.194
Yes, so Paul quietly.

00:18:17.254 --> 00:18:19.895
I know Maria.

00:18:19.955 --> 00:18:23.158
Well, said the reporter.

00:18:23.218 --> 00:18:25.880
Somebody must go to our mother's funeral.

00:18:25.940 --> 00:18:28.612
We need a report about it for the paper.

00:18:28.673 --> 00:18:33.856
Why don't you go, Paul?

00:18:33.916 --> 00:18:39.492
Paul went to the funeral the next day.

00:18:39.552 --> 00:18:43.034
It was a long way to the church, but he walked.

00:18:43.094 --> 00:18:45.135
He wanted to think.

00:18:45.196 --> 00:18:48.227
Maria loved me, he thought.

00:18:48.287 --> 00:18:50.748
But she married another man.

00:18:50.808 --> 00:18:52.099
Why?

00:18:52.159 --> 00:18:54.680
Because she was afraid of her mother.

00:18:54.740 --> 00:18:58.162
But now her mother is dead.

00:18:58.222 --> 00:19:02.394
Paul was happy and he was sad.

00:19:02.454 --> 00:19:04.726
He was at the church now.

00:19:04.786 --> 00:19:06.796
Crowds of people were there.

00:19:06.856 --> 00:19:08.755
It was a big funeral.

00:19:08.815 --> 00:19:12.926
There were many big black cars outside the church.

00:19:12.986 --> 00:19:15.708
In the first one was the coffin.

00:19:15.769 --> 00:19:20.522
There were a lot of flowers on the coffin and on the roof of the car.

00:19:20.582 --> 00:19:23.374
Paul stood at the back of the crowd.

00:19:23.434 --> 00:19:25.966
He took out his pencil and paper.

00:19:26.027 --> 00:19:28.960
He wrote about the cars and the people.

00:19:29.020 --> 00:19:32.412
Then he saw Maria.

00:19:32.472 --> 00:19:35.164
She was wearing a black dress.

00:19:35.224 --> 00:19:38.947
She looked sad, but very beautiful.

00:19:39.007 --> 00:19:41.308
She was standing alone.

00:19:41.368 --> 00:19:43.490
Nobody spoke to her.

00:19:43.550 --> 00:19:45.880
Nobody went near her.

00:19:45.941 --> 00:19:49.112
The man next to Paul spoke.

00:19:49.173 --> 00:19:51.894
That's the daughter, he said.

00:19:51.954 --> 00:19:53.716
She's a bad woman.

00:19:53.776 --> 00:19:56.577
She left her husband and it killed her mother.

00:19:56.637 --> 00:19:57.948
Look at her.

00:19:58.008 --> 00:20:00.713
Nobody wants to speak to her.

00:20:00.774 --> 00:20:03.069
Paul said nothing.

00:20:03.129 --> 00:20:05.620
Paul Maria, he thought.

00:20:05.680 --> 00:20:08.362
Everybody went inside the church.

00:20:08.422 --> 00:20:12.564
The funeral began.

00:20:12.625 --> 00:20:17.488
After the funeral, Paul went home.

00:20:17.548 --> 00:20:19.838
His mother was smiling.

00:20:19.898 --> 00:20:22.740
Good news, Paul, she said.

00:20:22.800 --> 00:20:25.062
Do you remember your cousin Elsa?

00:20:25.122 --> 00:20:27.513
Well, she's coming to stay with us.

00:20:27.573 --> 00:20:31.010
She's seventeen now, and very pretty.

00:20:31.070 --> 00:20:33.218
You will like her?"

00:20:33.278 --> 00:20:37.489
Yes, I remember Elsa, said Paul.

00:20:37.549 --> 00:20:39.570
He did not look pleased.

00:20:39.630 --> 00:20:42.251
His mother was disappointed.

00:20:42.312 --> 00:20:46.244
He's still thinking about Maria, she thought.

00:20:46.304 --> 00:20:48.966
Elsa will help him to forget.

00:20:49.026 --> 00:20:52.308
But Paul did not want to see Elsa.

00:20:52.368 --> 00:20:56.009
I must see Maria, he said to himself.

00:20:56.069 --> 00:21:08.290
I must talk to her.

00:21:08.350 --> 00:21:20.740
Part 4.

00:21:20.800 --> 00:21:23.722
Paul wanted to see Maria.

00:21:23.782 --> 00:21:26.173
He wanted to talk to her.

00:21:26.234 --> 00:21:29.625
I'll go to the house on the hill, he thought.

00:21:29.686 --> 00:21:32.288
Perhaps Maria will be there.

00:21:32.348 --> 00:21:35.420
But the house on the hill looked empty.

00:21:35.480 --> 00:21:38.061
There were no curtains at the windows.

00:21:38.121 --> 00:21:40.342
There was a big notice on the gate.

00:21:40.402 --> 00:21:43.144
It said, for sale.

00:21:43.204 --> 00:21:45.713
Paul looked over the gate.

00:21:45.773 --> 00:21:47.910
There was nobody in the garden.

00:21:47.970 --> 00:21:50.291
Everything was quiet."

00:21:50.351 --> 00:21:54.632
I'll get into the house and look round, he thought.

00:21:54.692 --> 00:21:57.152
Perhaps I'll find Maria's address.

00:21:57.212 --> 00:21:59.282
Then I can write to her.

00:21:59.342 --> 00:22:03.923
Paul pushed open the gate and went up the steps to the house.

00:22:03.983 --> 00:22:06.044
It was very quiet.

00:22:06.104 --> 00:22:08.404
He pushed at the front door.

00:22:08.464 --> 00:22:10.234
It was closed.

00:22:10.294 --> 00:22:12.095
He walked round the house.

00:22:12.115 --> 00:22:14.764
There was a window open.

00:22:14.824 --> 00:22:18.426
Quickly, Paul climbed through the open window.

00:22:18.486 --> 00:22:22.210
He was excited, and his heart was beating fast.

00:22:22.270 --> 00:22:24.992
He was in Maria's old home.

00:22:25.052 --> 00:22:27.104
He remembered her mother.

00:22:27.164 --> 00:22:30.046
He remembered that terrible evening.

00:22:30.106 --> 00:22:32.418
But the house was different now.

00:22:32.478 --> 00:22:34.669
There was no furniture in the room.

00:22:34.729 --> 00:22:37.051
There were no carpets and pictures.

00:22:37.111 --> 00:22:38.862
It was empty.

00:22:38.923 --> 00:22:41.974
Paul felt a little afraid.

00:22:42.034 --> 00:22:45.391
Is anybody in the house, he thought?

00:22:45.451 --> 00:22:46.975
No.

00:22:47.035 --> 00:22:49.356
He did not hear anything.

00:22:49.416 --> 00:22:54.297
Quietly, Paul went to the door of the room and opened it.

00:22:54.357 --> 00:22:56.328
There was nobody there.

00:22:56.388 --> 00:22:58.938
He went from room to room.

00:22:58.999 --> 00:23:03.220
All the rooms were big, and they were all empty.

00:23:03.280 --> 00:23:07.021
At last, he came to a very big room.

00:23:07.081 --> 00:23:08.681
He stopped.

00:23:08.741 --> 00:23:10.642
He knew this room.

00:23:10.702 --> 00:23:13.282
He had met Maria's mother here.

00:23:13.342 --> 00:23:15.508
He remembered everything.

00:23:15.568 --> 00:23:20.976
The old woman, her hard face, the big rings on her hands.

00:23:21.036 --> 00:23:24.338
And now the old woman was dead.

00:23:24.398 --> 00:23:27.622
Suddenly, Paul heard a noise.

00:23:27.682 --> 00:23:30.353
Somebody was inside the room.

00:23:30.413 --> 00:23:32.334
The door opened.

00:23:32.394 --> 00:23:35.316
Somebody was standing in the doorway.

00:23:35.376 --> 00:23:37.438
It was a woman.

00:23:37.498 --> 00:23:39.189
Maria!

00:23:39.249 --> 00:23:40.610
said Paul.

00:23:40.670 --> 00:23:41.911
Paul!

00:23:41.971 --> 00:23:45.190
Maria said, what are you doing here?

00:23:45.250 --> 00:23:48.590
I was looking for you, said Paul.

00:23:48.650 --> 00:23:51.933
You were looking for me, asked Maria.

00:23:51.994 --> 00:23:53.805
She smiled.

00:23:53.865 --> 00:23:56.558
Maria, said Paul.

00:23:56.618 --> 00:23:59.310
Why did you marry that man?

00:23:59.370 --> 00:24:02.242
Mother was old, said Maria.

00:24:02.302 --> 00:24:04.094
I was unhappy here.

00:24:04.154 --> 00:24:07.406
I never went to parties, never went out.

00:24:07.466 --> 00:24:09.478
I wanted money.

00:24:09.538 --> 00:24:13.125
I wanted a good time and friends.

00:24:13.184 --> 00:24:16.409
I understand," Paul said.

00:24:16.469 --> 00:24:18.480
You were not afraid of your mother.

00:24:18.540 --> 00:24:20.280
You were tired of her.

00:24:20.340 --> 00:24:23.852
She was old, and you wanted a new life.

00:24:23.912 --> 00:24:26.742
But why did you leave your husband?

00:24:26.802 --> 00:24:31.634
My husband, said Maria, that fat old man.

00:24:31.694 --> 00:24:33.655
He was stupid, Paul.

00:24:33.715 --> 00:24:35.015
He gave me money.

00:24:35.035 --> 00:24:39.046
He gave me jewels, a car, everything.

00:24:39.106 --> 00:24:41.478
But he didn't like my friends.

00:24:41.538 --> 00:24:43.379
He liked old people.

00:24:43.439 --> 00:24:47.192
I like clever, young people, Paul.

00:24:47.252 --> 00:24:48.914
I like you.

00:24:48.974 --> 00:24:51.324
You understand, don't you?"

00:24:51.384 --> 00:24:54.747
Yes, said Paul slowly.

00:24:54.807 --> 00:24:57.008
I understand now.

00:24:57.068 --> 00:24:59.680
I'm glad, said Maria.

00:24:59.740 --> 00:25:02.012
I was unhappy about you, Paul.

00:25:02.072 --> 00:25:03.442
I liked you.

00:25:03.502 --> 00:25:06.104
I liked your funny poems.

00:25:06.164 --> 00:25:09.976
My funny poems, said Paul.

00:25:10.036 --> 00:25:11.929
He stopped.

00:25:11.989 --> 00:25:14.652
You loved me, didn't you, Paul?

00:25:14.712 --> 00:25:16.032
Said Maria.

00:25:16.092 --> 00:25:18.304
Do you still love me?

00:25:18.364 --> 00:25:21.465
You are married, said Paul.

00:25:21.525 --> 00:25:23.606
You have a husband.

00:25:23.666 --> 00:25:26.988
But I don't love him, said Maria quickly.

00:25:27.048 --> 00:25:28.738
I want to be free.

00:25:28.798 --> 00:25:31.830
I want to go to parties and enjoy myself.

00:25:31.890 --> 00:25:33.160
Come with me.

00:25:33.220 --> 00:25:34.711
I have money now.

00:25:34.771 --> 00:25:37.002
We'll be happy together.

00:25:37.062 --> 00:25:39.854
No, said Paul.

00:25:39.914 --> 00:25:41.414
No.

00:25:41.474 --> 00:25:43.476
Everything's over.

00:25:43.536 --> 00:25:45.528
Maria was angry.

00:25:45.588 --> 00:25:51.022
Her eyes were small and cold, and her mouth was thin and hard.

00:25:51.082 --> 00:25:54.084
Her hands were covered with big rings.

00:25:54.144 --> 00:25:57.507
Maria looked like her mother.

00:25:57.567 --> 00:26:00.510
I'm sorry, Maria, he said.

00:26:00.570 --> 00:26:02.652
I don't love you anymore.

00:26:02.712 --> 00:26:07.565
I loved you very much, but now everything is different.

00:26:07.625 --> 00:26:09.416
Goodbye, Maria.

00:26:09.476 --> 00:26:11.520
But you can't leave me.

00:26:11.580 --> 00:26:14.673
Said Maria, I want you!

00:26:14.734 --> 00:26:19.076
Go back to your husband, said Paul.

00:26:19.136 --> 00:26:21.957
He looked at her for the last time.

00:26:22.017 --> 00:26:25.448
Then he turned and walked out of the room.

00:26:25.508 --> 00:26:29.170
Paul left the house on the hill and walked home.

00:26:29.230 --> 00:26:31.432
He was free.

00:26:31.492 --> 00:26:34.353
I was a fool, he thought.

00:26:34.413 --> 00:26:36.334
Maria never loved me.

00:26:36.394 --> 00:26:38.585
How stupid I was.

00:26:38.645 --> 00:26:40.582
Maria is beautiful.

00:26:40.642 --> 00:26:43.209
but she is hard and cold.

00:26:43.269 --> 00:26:45.560
She is like her mother.

00:26:45.620 --> 00:26:52.273
I loved Maria's beauty, but I never loved Maria.

00:26:52.333 --> 00:26:55.904
It was a lovely evening.

00:26:55.964 --> 00:26:58.205
Paul felt very happy.

00:26:58.265 --> 00:27:01.196
The door of the little brown house was open.

00:27:01.256 --> 00:27:03.047
His mother was at home.

00:27:03.107 --> 00:27:05.828
She was talking to a pretty girl.

00:27:05.888 --> 00:27:10.550
Paul, she said, this is your cousin Elsa.

00:27:10.610 --> 00:27:13.386
Hello, Elsa, said Paul.

00:27:13.446 --> 00:27:23.950
He smiled.

00:27:24.010 --> 00:27:42.071
The House on the Hill was read by Simon Maddox, and the recording produced by James Richardson at Studio AVP London.

